    "title": "Yesterday&#8217;s comments of note",
    "summary": "A few of the comments that stood out to us yesterday: \"This was my Dad’s car. I learned to drive a stick in this car and took my drivers test for my license. He and I worked on it together and we would race through the mountains. When he was over seas, my mom and I had to drive it weekly to keep it running. both of my parents are in heaven. My mom is looking down at me, saying what in the hell are you thinking? My dad is looking down at me and saying hell yeah!\" 86 joedryden commented on Korman-Built, S38-Powered Widebody 1968 BMW 1600ti 5-Speed \"It's bittersweet to see this car listed here with @craterface. I was the co-driver for the Modena Centro Ore event in this car and it was just a champion. In addition to buying a tested and regularly driven car, you are buying a top-tier seller. I've had the pleasure of over a decade of friendship with the seller and his is a dedicated, knowledgeable, and passionate steward of his cars. He is especially fond of Alfas and I suspect there is another Alfa coming to replace this one. Bid with&#8230;\" 13 deichenb commented on 1957 Alfa Romeo Giulietta Sprint \"Leading off the BaT Best Flybys of the Week is #XS003. The Kenny Brown suspension and chassis mods really hook this car up. Trust me when I tell you that this Outlaw is capable of so much more. https://www.facebook.com/share/r/18zchQUvvz/ https://www.instagram.com/reel/DblPO8YDVzQ/?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet \" 12 campari commented on One-Family-Owned, 30k-Mile 1992 Ford Mustang Kenny Brown Outlaw XS \"I was calm and collected, until I saw your congrats posts. I just got emotional I have dreamed of owning this car for 30 years, and this is my 50th birthday gift to myself. super excited\" 11 TShab commented on 1991 Acura NSX",
